# round 122 (w139), REBUILT: 027's own backbone, hidden 90, nine attention heads, two transformer blocks. The first build used hidden 48 with four heads and every cell died in the graph regularizer (jobs 2757, 2758): its configuration pins the nine gene graphs to heads 0 to 8 of the SECOND block, so a one-block cell never evaluates the term (graph_reg_loss 0.0 for all 200 epochs of w134_bxctx s2700) and a two-block cell with four heads indexes a head it does not have. This is round 8's finding, job 2261. bxwide and aawide are therefore the affine-free controls on the backbone 020 and 027 actually trained, where the regularizer does fire; paired against w134_bxctx and w135_aactx.
